## Summary

**Root cause of the attempt-1 gate failure** (not a Lean error): the gate runs `lake env lean <abs path>` with `cwd = worktree root`. The D5/D6 scaffold placed the lake project only in `release/`, so the worktree root had no `lean-toolchain`/`lakefile.toml`/`.lake`; `elan` aborted with `no default toolchain configured` before Lean ever started, for every file. (The attempt-1 `gate.json` had already been deleted by `dispatch_loop.write_repair_prompt`, so I reproduced the command to recover stderr.)

**Fix (gate scaffold only — zero mathematical content changed):** the worktree root now carries the same root-level lake project layout as the previously verified D1–D4 worktrees:
- `lakefile.toml`, `lake-manifest.json`, `lean-toolchain` — byte-identical copies of the `release/` versions (mathlib rev `7974e751`)
- `.lake -> release/.lake` — shares the package store and already-built outputs

